From a0f8d24142e802c5e72df7200a2366e72036cc40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linya14x <linx.yang@intel.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:06:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] staging: ipu7: Defer ISYS frame-drop logging

Printing frame-drop messages directly inside the interrupt handler (ISR)
can introduce significant latency and CPU overhead, especially during
frequent frame drops or drop storms.

To address this, defer frame-drop logging to a delayed workqueue:
1. Aggregate frame-drop counts on a per-stream basis and periodically
   output the latest error details from process context once per second.
2. Store only 'struct ia_gofo_msg_err' instead of the full response
   structure, reducing hard-IRQ spinlock copy overhead from 64B+ to 24B
   and driver memory footprint from ~1.1KB to 384B.
3. Synchronously flush pending frame-drop logs upon closing a stream,
   entering runtime suspend, and removing the device, avoiding stale drop
   counts from contaminating subsequent streaming sessions or logging after
   hardware power-down.

Signed-off-by: linya14x <linx.yang@intel.com>
Change-Id: I0df07533effc4f93d70b8c98260227f7d30ed1a3
---
